# v1.0.1
## Minor
- Resolved bug that was preventing local storage templates from being configured fully for inns/banks
- Resolved a bug that was preventing template inn/storage combos from deploying smoothly(required reconfiguration on location creation).

# v1.0.0
## Major
- Price variations for merchants (Buying and selling)
- Price variation/refresh added to Inns
- Storage template Type added.
- "Cart" for purchases now allows for choosing who receives a purchased item.
- Storage Template rentals added to banks
- Storage template ties to rented room.
- Moved "Mark As Settlement" to Dedicated "Sandbox" tab, this will become standard for all DDF Sandbox Modules.


# v0.9.1
## Minor
- Local Merchant set up now properly handles limited stock formulas and availability
- Added a "Refresh Stock" button to merchants, Allowing GM's to trigger inventory restocks immediately.
# v0.9.0

## Major
- GM now can edit bank deposites (change amount/Maturity/move to a different character)
- GM can now Create/Edit Bookings on Inn's
- Item stacks when purchased now properly stack rather then entering inventory as # separate items.
- Unified merchant/bank/inn/sell data-building into a single shared module so the GM Settlement Manager and the player location window always behave identically (previously drifted copies).
- Added Loan creation ability for banks. Loans have an amount, interest, and interest period. Refinement needed.
- Changed Settlement manager stock/inventory system to now open a localized template editing menu. Giving local settlement editing full capabilities of the system, and unifying the setup process, rather then maintaining two different configuration processes.

## Minor
- Fixed: Partial withdrawls of matured deposits were being handled incorrectly causing more money to be 
  withdrawn then requested, while still only givng characters the requested amount.
- Fixed: Deposites were being merged into the next highest denomination as they were withdrawn. 
  IE 10gp being withdrawn as 1pp
- Fixed: merchant stock is now tracked — buying an item reduces its quantity, sold-out items can't be bought,
  and checkout is blocked (no charge) when a cart exceeds available stock. Duplicate buys merge into one capped cart line.
- Fixed: player deposits/withdrawals sent over the socket are now processed 
  (payload was previously mis-routed and silently dropped).
- Security: bank deposit/withdrawal socket handlers now verify the requesting player owns the target actor.
- Player shop view now hides sold-out items and auto-selects a default bank actor, matching the GM window.
- Inn random-menu draws now respect the min/max draw range in both windows.
- Performance: world-time updates re-render open windows on a debounce instead of every tick; item lookups cached per render.
- Restock/menu save failures are now logged instead of silently swallowed.

